.\" Title: vrw-resize
.\" Author: vrw contributors
.\" Manual section: 1
.\" Process this file with
.\"   groff -man -Tascii vrw-resize.1

.TH VRW\-RESIZE 1 "2025" "vrw" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
vrw\-resize \- resize the virtual terminal of a running command

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vrw
\fBresize\fR [\fITARGET\fR] [\fB\-\-rows\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-cols\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-interactive\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
Resize the virtual terminal (VTTY) of a running command. This resizes both the in-memory terminal buffer and the child process's PTY (by sending SIGWINCH), so applications that respond to terminal resize events (like vim, htop, or less) will adjust their layout accordingly.

When \fB\-\-rows\fR and \fB\-\-cols\fR are both omitted (or set to 0), vrw auto-detects the terminal size from the controlling terminal using \fB$COLUMNS\fR and \fB$LINES\fR environment variables, or falls back to \fBstty size\fR. When only one dimension is specified, the other is auto-detected.

The target can be specified as an OS PID (numeric) or a command name/ID string. Name matching follows the same three-round strategy as \fBstop-command\fR: exact match, prefix on full display string, prefix on name only.

Valid ranges: rows 1\-200, cols 1\-500.

.SH ARGUMENTS

.TP
.B TARGET
OS PID (numeric) or command name of the command to resize.

.SH OPTIONS

.TP
.BR "\-\-rows " \fIN\fR
New terminal height in rows (1\-200, default: auto-detect from controlling terminal).

.TP
.BR "\-\-cols " \fIN\fR
New terminal width in columns (1\-500, default: auto-detect from controlling terminal).

.TP
.BR \-\-interactive
Present a numbered list of commands and let the user select
which ones to resize by typing space-separated numbers (e.g. "1 3 5").
Requires a terminal (stdin must be a TTY).

.SH EXAMPLES

.PP
Resize to explicit dimensions:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrw resize abc123 \-\-rows 40 \-\-cols 120\fR
Resized command with PID 5678 to 40x120 on instance 12345 (PID 12345)
.fi
.RE

.PP
Auto-detect from current terminal:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrw resize abc123\fR
Resized command with PID 5678 to 50x200 on instance 12345 (PID 12345)
.fi
.RE

.PP
Resize by OS PID:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrw resize 5678 \-\-rows 30 \-\-cols 100\fR
Resized command with PID 5678 to 30x100 on instance 12345 (PID 12345)
.fi
.RE

.PP
Resize by name:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrw resize vim \-\-rows 60 \-\-cols 200\fR
Resized command with PID 5679 to 60x200 on instance 12345 (PID 12345)
.fi
.RE

.PP
Equivalent curl:
.RS
.PP
.nf
curl -s -X POST "http://localhost:9090/api/commands/abc123/resize" \e
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \e
  -d '{"rows": 40, "cols": 120}'
.fi
.RE

.SH EXIT STATUS

.TP
.B 0
Terminal resized successfully.

.TP
.B 1
Error (command not found, resize failed, out of range, etc.).

.SH SEE ALSO

.BR vrw (1),
.BR vrw\-list (1),
.BR vrw\-spawn (1),
.BR vrwctrl (1)
